FALKORDB_HOST=falkordb #This is the hostname or IP address of the FalkorDB service. In this case, it is set to "falkordb", which is likely the name of the service in a Docker Compose setup. You can change this to the appropriate hostname or IP address where your FalkorDB instance is running.
FALKORDB_PORT=6379 #This is the port number on which the FalkorDB service is running. The default port for FalkorDB is 6379, but you can change it if your FalkorDB instance is configured to use a different port.
FALKORDB_GRAPH=cause-loom #This is the name of the graph in FalkorDB that will be used for storing and retrieving data related to the CauseLoom application. You can change this to any valid graph name as per your requirements.

OPENAI_API_KEY=your-key-here #This is the API key for accessing OpenAI's services. You need to replace "your-key-here" with your actual OpenAI API key. Make sure to keep this key secure and do not share it publicly.
OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4.1-mini #This specifies the OpenAI model to be used for generating responses. In this case, it is set to "gpt-4.1-mini", which is a smaller version of the GPT-4 model. You can change this to any other available model as per your requirements.

CAUSELOOM_SEED_ENABLED=true #This flag indicates whether the CauseLoom application should seed the database with initial data. If set to "true", the application will populate the database with sample data on startup. If set to "false", it will not seed the database.
CAUSELOOM_DEMO_ENABLED=true #This flag indicates whether the CauseLoom application should simulate outage of services for demonstration purposes.
